            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आभो (ābho) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from abhra, \"cloud, rainy weather\". CDIAL lists Old Marwari ābhai under it (CDIAL 549). The Old Marwari row means \"in the sky\"; Gujarati ābh means \"sky, clouds\"."
            }
